 ],
 "text": "Jack nodded once. The number felt different now. It was no longer a population statistic in a planning report. It was every sleeping family, every night-shift technician, every child, every patient, and every person who would wake to a world that no longer fit them.\n\nJack looked through the window again at the impossible forest beyond the streetlights. Forty-three people, their homes, laboratories, vehicles, and everything else inside the TOMBS boundary had been caught in the same event.\n\nSarah reached for his hand."
